Now, let me re-answer some with mild spoilers:

> 1)  Is there any possible way to ingest gold?
Yes, some monsters do.

> 2)  Is it possible to bury gold using the pick-axe?
Yes, it's possible to bury most things by digging with a pick-axe,
then dropping things in the hole, then pushing a boulder on top.  But
there's not much point to burying gold.  It's safe enough if you just
drop it in a chest.

> 3)  Is it possible to melt gold?  So far I have not been able to do
> it.
No (although I haven't tried dropping it in lava.  I don't think it
would be useful in any case)

> 4)  Lastly, does #dipping coins or dropping coins in fountains change
> my luck at all?
No.  There are betting things to do with gold, and better things to do
with fountains.





Now with stronger spoilers.  Stop reading now.  But in case you
don't...

> 1)  Is there any possible way to ingest gold?
Yes, but not much point.  You could polymorph into a monster that eats
gold (rock mole, Xorn), and then eat it.  But it doesn't help much.
Now eating other golden things might help.  Like, for example, a spare
ring of teleport control, if it happen to be made of gold while you
were polymorphed into a Xorn...

> 2)  Is it possible to bury gold using the pick-axe?
Yes, it's possible to bury most things by digging with a pick-axe,
then dropping things in the hole, then pushing a boulder on top.  But
there's not much point to burying gold.  It's safe enough if you just
drop it in a chest.

The only useful thing to bury (which occurs to me) is troll corpses,
to stop them from resurecting.  But it's normally easier to throw them
in a bag.  If you detect gold with gold-detection, and can't see it
when you get there, it could be buried.  You can dig it up with a pick-
axe.  But it might also be a monster was carrying it when you used
gold-detection, and the monster moved.

> 4)  Lastly, does #dipping coins or dropping coins in fountains change
> my luck at all?

No.  The main things to do with a fountain are dip long swords (if
you're lawful and at least level 5), or quaff from them.  Dipping
cursed items sometimes uncurses them.  There are some other nice
effects too, particularly if you're lucky, and the fountain is magic,
you may get "gain ability".  However, playing with fountains can cause
problems, and can easily kill an early character.

Early on, gold is main useful for buying things from shops, if you
don't want to waste time getting your pet to steal from the shop.  As
you go on in the game (say past level 20), you won't find that too
useful, and you'll probably have way too much gold.  The only
significant thing you can do is... Well, you didn't want spoilers
right?  What about a fortune cookie?  Here's one:

